// Stages three and four replace modest upgrades with changes to the whole body.
export const DEEP_GROWTH = {
  antlers:['The antlers branch behind your ears and down the back of your neck. You feel each new fork before it hardens. Turning your head turns a whole crown of pale wood, wide enough that the people beside you move their chairs.','The crown keeps growing until its lowest branches brace against your shoulders. Small leaves unfold above you. You duck through an arch and feel every leaf brush the frame, as distinctly as fingers.'],
  fox:['Copper fur runs down your jaw and over your shoulders. Your nose lengthens beneath your checking fingers; your teeth no longer meet where you expect. A laugh escapes as a sharp bark. You swallow the next one.','Your face settles into a long, fine muzzle. Fur covers your scalp and neck, but the brass clip stays caught above one ear. You say your name carefully around the changed shape of your mouth. Both ears lean toward the sound.'],
  halo:['The rings widen through your shoulders and waist. Your body hangs inside their slow rotation, heels barely touching the floor. You grab the chair to pull yourself down. The chair lifts instead.','One ring turns through your ribs without opening them. Another circles your knees. You float at their common center, carried by machinery you cannot put a hand on. Walking now requires persuading the rings to follow the floor.'],
  honey:['The softness passes your elbows and keeps going. Your ribs give beneath your hands; your legs pool together before you can spread your feet. You pull yourself upright from a single amber column, frightened by how easily your body obeys.','Your outline pours down into a deep amber pool. You can feel the floor across its whole surface. When you reach for the counter, a shoulder, an arm, and a familiar face rise out of it together. Holding that shape takes attention. Letting it flow does not.'],
  porcelain:['The glaze closes over your chest and back. Beneath it, the weight of flesh gives way to a hollow chamber. You knock against your sternum and hear the note travel from your throat to your ankles.','Your torso rounds into a great porcelain vessel. One arm can still make a hand; the other folds into a curved handle when you lose concentration. You press against your side and hear yourself ring. You do not let anyone else try it.'],
  stars:['The lights beneath your skin pull apart into depth. You can see through your chest into a distance the room has no space for. Your fingers look like a constellation joined by thin lines of darkness.','Your outline comes loose from the stars inside it. For a moment there is no skin to locate, only lights choosing the arrangement of a person. You gather them around the familiar position of your face. Your freckles are the brightest points.'],
  velvet:['The note leaves your throat and settles through your whole body. You feel it in your palms when you speak, and in the table where they rest. People answer before you finish asking. You start choosing your words more carefully.','You open your mouth and the room seems to breathe with you. Your voice comes from every surface you touch. You lift your hands off the counter, testing whether the silence belongs to you too.'],
  bells:['The bells spread through your ribs in a succession of cool, bright weights. Every step strikes a chord. You hold yourself still, but your next breath rings the smallest bell all by itself.','Your chest opens into an airy frame of suspended bells. You see them move beneath the outline of your shirt. Your thoughts arrive through their motion; to say a word, you have to let the whole frame answer.'],
  echo:['Two versions of you answer the next question. You hear the one you refuse fade across the room. For a moment you can see her mouth moving beside yours in the glass.','Your reflection acts a full sentence ahead. A second outline lingers behind your shoulders, finishing the answer you abandoned. You have to choose which voice to follow before your body knows where to stand.'],
  moth:['A second pair of wings unfolds below the first. The new muscles travel down your back into your hips. You stop trying to fit in the chair and hover beside it, four great fans keeping you level.','Your legs draw together beneath a soft, segmented body. A pale ruff grows around your throat. You hang in the air on four broad wings, hands tucked close while your new balance settles. The lamp feels near even across the room.'],
  clockwork:['The little clicks climb through your elbows and into your shoulders. Brass struts fit beneath your chest; winding pressure replaces the ordinary pull of muscle. You can stop halfway through a breath and stay there.','Your torso opens along a neat brass seam. Gears turn behind your ribs, keeping time with a movement you recognize as your heartbeat. You close the seam with both thumbs. The key at your back keeps turning.'],
  ribbons:['The ribbons divide past your shoulders. Your torso loosens into a broad weave that can pass between the chair rungs. You pull it together quickly, but your outline has already learned another way to fit.','You come apart into long green lengths. Each one carries sensation along its full span. You braid a face, two arms, and something close to a waist out of the moving bundle, then catch the stray end that keeps trying to reach the dice.'],
  tail:['Your tail divides with a slow pull at the base of your spine. Three copper lengths fan out behind you. They catch your balance together, then disagree about which chair leg to curl around.','Nine tails open behind you, broad enough to hide the chair. You try to count them by touch and feel all nine answers at once. One lifts your cup while another catches the handle before it can spill.'],
  shadow:['Your shadow lifts from the floor and stands beside you. You can see through it, but you feel its hand when it catches your sleeve. Your own body looks thinner wherever the two of you separate.','Half the weight leaves you. Your shadow takes it and becomes a second dark body, joined to yours by a narrow strip at the heels. You cannot quite agree which of you is standing under the light.'],
  roots:['The roots thicken until your feet lift inside a moving tangle. Bark grows over your calves. You cross the room on many small, searching points, feeling the floor long before your eyes reach it.','Your legs join into a low trunk carried by a spreading root system. New shoots climb your back. You have to gather several feet of yourself before moving, and the floor keeps calling through every tip you leave behind.'],
};

